## Sample Problem Types

### **Problem Type 1: API Response Transformation & Validation**

**Description:** Parse a cooking suggestion from an AI API and transform it into your application's schema. Validate that required fields exist and handle missing/malformed data gracefully.

**Challenge:** The AI API returns unstructured text. You need to parse it into a structured Recipe object.

```javascript
// Input from AI API
const aiResponse = `
Here's a recipe for pasta:
- Ingredients: 400g pasta, 2 cups tomato sauce, garlic
- Instructions: Cook pasta. Heat sauce. Mix together.
- Time: 20 minutes
`;

// Expected output
const expectedRecipe = {
  title: "Pasta with Tomato Sauce",
  ingredients: [
    { name: "pasta", amount: 400, unit: "g" },
    { name: "tomato sauce", amount: 2, unit: "cups" },
    { name: "garlic", amount: null, unit: null }
  ],
  instructions: ["Cook pasta", "Heat sauce", "Mix together"],
  cookTime: 20,
  servings: 2
};

// Solution approach:
class RecipeParser {
  static parse(aiText) {
    // 1. Use regex or AI-assisted parsing to extract sections
    // 2. Map each ingredient to structured format
    // 3. Validate required fields
    // 4. Return Recipe instance or throw ValidationError
  }

  static validate(recipe) {
    if (!recipe.title) throw new ValidationError("Title required");
    if (!Array.isArray(recipe.ingredients) || recipe.ingredients.length === 0) {
      throw new ValidationError("At least one ingredient required");
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

